  get seen and behind it there was a  gigantic mechanism called the crane in  fact our word machine mechanic comes  from the Greek word for crane Makani  because this crane was one of the most  impressive pieces of machinery and  engineering in the Greek world and it  was applied as so much of our technology  is not to warfare or to commerce but to  the entertainment industry these cranes  would lift up actors swing them up and  over the roof of the skinny building the  scene building and hang them out over  the stage to the left and the right were  the chorus with their separate entrances  each one called a parados in front of  them spread the tiers of seats that they  could look out to and then speaking as  gods they would declaimed the end of the  play they would wrap up the action they  would deal out fates and fortunes to the  various principal characters of the  drama in Latin the word for one of these  figures flown in on the great crane was  deus ex machina god from the machine and  so we still use that phrase today for  any work of art be it a movie or a stage  play or a novel that drags in by the  hair of its head without any proper  reason for being rationale someone who  will with the twinkling of an eye and  the wave of a wand fix whatever the  dramatic problem is so that the work of  art can end that's our deus ex machina  but for the Greeks it was a moment of  Epiphany a words which means shining  forth as the God appeared floating  flying above the stage in what must have  been some of the most dramatic moments  anyone has ever seen in a theatre you  can play a role at Epidaurus there's an  International Folk Festival on that site  every day that it's open to tourists go  out to the sweet spot in the center of  the circle today marked by a stone take  your turn and then stand there as many  others will have stood before you and do  what they have done sing a song  recite a poem express feelings for a  distant loved one but speak your piece  you too will have the thrill of knowing  that your friends up in the tears are  hearing that magic acoustic carry your  ordinary normal tone of voice way up to  the very top of this great theater
 

